review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.md:73:The EXTREME-RANK-PRESERVE variant keeps every unique v6 rank (49 values) but maps them all OUTSIDE [0.2, 0.8]. Ensemble gain is **+4.68 pp** — even higher than v6 original's +4.53 pp. Middle-mass is 0% but rank granularity is preserved.
review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.md:75:Meanwhile my median-BIN transformation collapsed 49 ranks to 2, which is why ensemble dropped. **The 2.2pp drop was from rank collapse, not middle-mass loss.**
review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.md:79:- Paper abstract previously claimed middle-zone mass is the mechanism. This is **wrong**: middle-mass is correlated with rank granularity but not causal.
review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.md:80:- The correct mechanism is **rank granularity**: Direct has 11 unique values (coarse bimodal grid); v6 has 49 (fine). Averaging breaks ties in Direct's coarse clusters with real signal.
review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.md:84:1. Rewrote abstract "Mechanism" paragraph: middle-mass → rank granularity; explicitly cited v6-EXT-RANK and v6-AFFINE results.
review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.md:86:3. Updated v8 secondary-contribution paragraph: v8's smaller gain is now explained by rank-granularity collapse (few unique values) instead of middle-mass.
review-stage/AUTO_REVIEW.md:90:Codex reviewer will retry at 08:05 CST (credit limit reset). Round 3 will re-submit the corrected paper and request a final score.
