refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18_v7.md:3719:Domain slices produce labels like `domain=D5c`, but the v7 prompt explicitly says the agent has no domain information. `direct_margin` requires knowing a separate Direct model score. `tool_used=True`, `tool_used=False`, and `n_turns>=2` are post-treatment behavioral slices, not input conditions. `subspacead_rank` is only known after calling `tool_expert_score`.
refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18_v7.md:3761:The script tests roughly 21 slices per tool: 12 domains plus margin/tool-used/rank/turn slices. With CI lower > 0 from a two-sided 95% bootstrap, the positive-side null false-positive rate is about 2.5% per valid slice. Expected false positive niches are about `21 * 0.025 = 0.53` per tool, or `13 * 21 * 0.025 = 6.8` across 13 tools. Probability of at least one false positive across all tools is effectively near certain under independence; correlations reduce or reshape this, but do not solve snooping.
refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18_v7.md:3809:5. Run an ablation matrix on test only after freezing: Direct, v7 prompt with no tools, v7 tools without hints, v7 hints without KEEP gate, and full v7. This separates prompt effects from actual tool utility.
refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18_v7.md:3840:Domain slices produce labels like `domain=D5c`, but the v7 prompt explicitly says the agent has no domain information. `direct_margin` requires knowing a separate Direct model score. `tool_used=True`, `tool_used=False`, and `n_turns>=2` are post-treatment behavioral slices, not input conditions. `subspacead_rank` is only known after calling `tool_expert_score`.
refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18_v7.md:3882:The script tests roughly 21 slices per tool: 12 domains plus margin/tool-used/rank/turn slices. With CI lower > 0 from a two-sided 95% bootstrap, the positive-side null false-positive rate is about 2.5% per valid slice. Expected false positive niches are about `21 * 0.025 = 0.53` per tool, or `13 * 21 * 0.025 = 6.8` across 13 tools. Probability of at least one false positive across all tools is effectively near certain under independence; correlations reduce or reshape this, but do not solve snooping.
refine-logs/CODEX_REVIEW_2026-04-18_v7.md:3930:5. Run an ablation matrix on test only after freezing: Direct, v7 prompt with no tools, v7 tools without hints, v7 hints without KEEP gate, and full v7. This separates prompt effects from actual tool utility.
