review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1281:3. Score-distribution explanation: Direct is 100% bimodal (0% in [0.2, 0.8]); v6 has 24% middle-zone mass; v8 has 0.4%. Ensemble gain correlates monotonically with middle-zone mass.
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1283:## Method: v8 refutation agent
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1286:1. Suspect list (turn 1, no tool): VLM outputs initial_score + up to 3 candidate_features (name, location, looks_defect_like) + refutation_target index
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1287:2. Targeted refutation (turn 2+): call side_by_side / reference_profiler / reference_retriever to find the candidate in refs; tool output has explicit "interpretation" with disconfirm clause
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1288:3. Verdict + update: refutation_verdict ∈ {found_in_ref, not_found, inconclusive}; remove refuted features from remaining list; updated_score
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1291:- Output bimodality (VLM emits extreme scores, capping ranking)
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1294:Theoretical twist: inverts default from "anomaly-until-confirmed" (v6 style) to "normal-until-survived-refutation" (v8 style). Each tool output has exactly one legitimate use — retiring a candidate — so the protocol is structurally biased toward ruling out.
