review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1960:"""Agent v8 — Skeptical-Verification Agent (refutation-driven).
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1963:specific anomaly and then commits. v8 inverts this: the agent treats the
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1965:by finding it in refs. Only features that resist refutation count as
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1968:Innovation claim: "Anomaly detection as refutation — every flagged feature
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1970:Tool calls are explicitly framed as refutation probes, not confirmation."
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1974:    - `initial_score`: gut anomaly score (like Direct).
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1980:      ("refutation_target") and call a tool that can show whether this
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:1984:    - `refutation_verdict`: did tool find the feature in refs?
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2014:    severity assessment, not refutation.)
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2032:    Returns subspacead normalized_rank. rank<=0.4 ⇒ query looks normal
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2033:    relative to the training distribution; rank>=0.85 ⇒ query's visual
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2056:You counter that bias by REQUIRING refutation probes on every suspicion.
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2068:    "refutation_target": index into candidate_features of the ONE feature
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2074:      the feature at refutation_target — i.e. show it in refs.
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2082:    "refutation_verdict": "found_in_ref"|"not_found"|"inconclusive"
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2090:    - Else if budget allows → pick next refutation_target and call next tool.
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2097:  - If you call tool_expert_score and rank>=0.85, this increases your prior
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2098:    but does NOT end the refutation step. You still need to check the
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2100:  - FP items where Direct is wrong typically have candidate_features that
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2103:  - FN items where Direct misses an anomaly typically have a single
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2112:  "refutation_target":            <int|null>,
review-stage/codex_review_r2_raw.out:2113:  "refutation_verdict":           "found_in_ref"|"not_found"|"inconclusive"|null,
