review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:14:# Round 1 of autonomous review loop
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:16:You are a senior ML reviewer at NeurIPS/ICML level. Score this work 1-10 for a top venue, identify remaining critical weaknesses, and state if it's READY for submission.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:22:**Topic**: VLM-based anomaly detection across 12 domains via a tool-using ReAct agent. Headline contribution: agent+Direct VLM score ensemble outperforms either alone, mechanistically explained by score-distribution diversity.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:27:   - Direct VLM: macro AUROC 0.7684
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:29:   - **v6 + Direct ensemble (0.5/0.5): 0.8136 (+4.53pp, 95% CI [+2.82, +6.31], p<0.001)**
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:30:   - v8 refutation agent + Direct (0.6/0.4): 0.7812 (+1.28pp, p=0.038)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:31:   - Triple blend 0.5 Direct + 0.1 v6 + 0.4 v8: 0.8036 (+3.52pp)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:34:   - Direct: 0.8153
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:36:   - v8 refutation: 0.7731 (-4.2pp)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:37:   - Best triple (0.5 d + 0.3 v66 + 0.2 v8): 0.8388 (+2.4pp)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:39:3. Score-distribution explanation: Direct is 100% bimodal (0% in [0.2, 0.8]); v6 has 24% middle-zone mass; v8 has 0.4%. Ensemble gain correlates monotonically with middle-zone mass.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:41:## Method: v8 refutation agent
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:44:1. Suspect list (turn 1, no tool): VLM outputs initial_score + up to 3 candidate_features (name, location, looks_defect_like) + refutation_target index
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:45:2. Targeted refutation (turn 2+): call side_by_side / reference_profiler / reference_retriever to find the candidate in refs; tool output has explicit "interpretation" with disconfirm clause
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:46:3. Verdict + update: refutation_verdict ∈ {found_in_ref, not_found, inconclusive}; remove refuted features from remaining list; updated_score
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:49:- Output bimodality (VLM emits extreme scores, capping ranking)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:52:Theoretical twist: inverts default from "anomaly-until-confirmed" (v6 style) to "normal-until-survived-refutation" (v8 style). Each tool output has exactly one legitimate use — retiring a candidate — so the protocol is structurally biased toward ruling out.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:56:### Abstract (v8-era rewrite)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:57:[paper/sections/0_abstract.tex — focuses on two failure modes, refutation agent, score-distribution diversity]
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:59:Key claim: "a simple 0.5·Direct + 0.5·v6-agent ensemble reaches macro AUROC 0.8136, beating the descriptor-only Direct VLM baseline (0.7684) by +4.52 pp (stratified paired bootstrap 95% CI [+2.82, +6.31], P(Δ>0)=1.000 on 1,418 items)."
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:61:### Method section 3.5 (new subsection on v8)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:69:- Finding 5: v6 agent + Direct ensemble = headline result
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:70:- Finding 6: v8 refutation agent as interpretable alternative (+1.28pp test)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:75:1. **v8's theoretical innovation doesn't translate to strongest ensemble gain.** v8 has cleaner refutation theory but +1.28pp test vs v6's +4.53pp. The gap is explained by score-distribution analysis: v8 pushes to binary (0.05 or 0.85), v6's looser JSON accidentally produces middle-zone diversity.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:76:2. **v8 GPT-5.4 test data incomplete.** sub2api rate-limited heavily; 85% JSON parse errors at test scale. GPT numbers are dev-only (n=480).
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:77:3. **v8 single-tool audits showed ALL tools DROP individually on dev.** Per-tool audit framework was run but produced null result (every tool hurts when forced as the only option). Useful as supporting evidence but not as main contribution.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:85:- `benchmark/scripts/agent_v8.py` — new refutation agent
