review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:477:Direct is 100% bimodal (no middle-zone scores). v6.5 naturally produces
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:478:24% middle-zone scores via its noisier JSON protocol. v8 — despite
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:479:the explicit refutation theory — still concentrates in extremes (0.4%
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:480:middle) because the protocol collapses to "all refuted → 0.05" or
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:483:**Why ensemble wins**: averaging a bimodal signal with a middle-mass
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:484:signal creates rank diversity. v6.5's accidental diversity gives
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:485:+4.5pp; v8's near-bimodal distribution gives +1.3pp.
