review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:507:forward pass. Adding v8 on top provides marginal +0.16pp.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:509:## Theory: "Refutation Agent" (v8)
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:511:Novel framing: anomaly detection as **explicit refutation**. The agent
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:518:"normal-until-survived-refutation". The protocol successfully flips
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:520:flips some correct FNs (D6 loses 17pp on test because tool refutation
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:523:**Why v8 doesn't beat v6.5 in ensemble**: the explicit protocol
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:525:the middle-zone diversity that makes v6.5 such a strong ensemble
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:530:1. **Score-distribution ensemble diversification** — framing that
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:531:   explains why agent+Direct ensemble dominates either alone.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:532:2. **Refutation agent as interpretable baseline** — v8 produces
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:533:   structured traces (candidate_features, refutation_verdicts,
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:543:   v8 method description + new test numbers.
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:545:   refutation with graded evidence weights) to preserve v8's theory
review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:546:   AND capture v6.5's score diversity. Hypothesis: v9+Direct > v6.5+Direct.
