review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:2992:A cleaner publishable version would say: “Training-free VAD benefits from score-diverse VLM-agent ensembling; the gain is explained by complementary rank structure, not stronger standalone agents.” Then back it with test-set results across at least two reliable backbones, strong simple baselines, controlled score-shape ablations, and a corrected v8 trace audit. With that package, this could move into a 6.5-7 range.

codex
The mechanism rewrite is present in the abstract and experiments, and the rank-preserving control now directly falsifies the old middle-mass claim. I’m checking for remaining internal contradictions now, especially stale v8 language and whether the main table still overclaims dev-only or weakly supported results.
